    <figcaption>
      <p>Hi, I’m Derron Yu, a <strong>Master of Finance candidate at the Rotman School of Management</strong> with a passion for <strong>markets, sustainable finance, and data-driven decision-making</strong>. My background in <strong>Economics, International Relations, and Statistics</strong> gives me a unique perspective on how financial systems connect to global trends, policy, and sustainability.</p>
      <p>Previously, as a <strong>Financial Analyst at University Health Network (UHN)</strong>, I managed multi-million-dollar research grants and clinical trial budgets, working closely with stakeholders to ensure financial sustainability in healthcare research.<br>Beyond finance, I’m a firm believer in using capital to drive <strong>sustainable and impactful change</strong>. I’ve competed in <strong>business case competitions</strong> focused on ESG and impact investing, consulted for sustainability-focused organizations, and co-founded a <strong>mental health nonprofit</strong> during the pandemic as part of a Harvard-led initiative.</p>
      <p>I’m always up for a conversation about <strong>markets, trading strategies, sustainable finance, or just great movies and thrifting finds.</strong></p>
      <p>Through my website, I hope you’ll be able to understand my skill set, diverse set of work experiences, and passion for a variety of fields including finance, sustainability, sports business, economics and gaming! Feel free to reach out through my various social media and professional platforms.</p>
    </figcaption>
